          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em compact Hausdorff space
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            which is both a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+space"} Hausdorff space
            as well as a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+space"} compact space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit+of+a+sequence"} limit
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequence"} sequence
            or more generally of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/net"} net
            that should exist does exist (
            %a{:href => "net#CompactSpacesEquivalentlyHaveConvergetSubnets"}> this prop.
            ) and does so uniquely (
            %a{:href => "#NetsDetectHausdorff"}> this prop
            ).
          %p
            One may consider the analogous condition for
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convergence+spaces"} convergence spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locales"} locales
            (see also at
            %em
              %a{:href => "Hausdorff+space#HausdorffLocale"} Hausdorff locale
            and
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+locale"} compact locale
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
          %p
          #Terminology.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %strong (Terminology)
              %br/
              In the literature, the term “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactum"}> compactum
              ” is sometimes used as a synonym for “compact Hausdorff space”. Be warned however that “compactum” is also frequently used to refer to “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+metrizable+spaces"}> compact metrizable spaces
              ”.
              %br/
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p
            If you know what a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+space"} compact space
            is and what a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+space"} Hausdorff space
            is, then you know what a compact Hausdorff space is, so let's be fancy. (Full justifications will be provided in section on
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a{:href => "#algebras"} compact Hausdorff spaces as algebras
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
