                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in \mu U \;\Leftrightarrow\; \{ F \in \beta S \;|\; A \in F \} \in U
              \.
          %p
            Then a
            %strong compact Hausdorff space
            is simply an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+for+a+monad"} algebra
            for this monad; that is, a set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            together with a function
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi lim
                    %mo :
                    %mi β
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lim: \beta X \to X
          %ul
            %li
              each point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              is the limit (
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi lim
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lim
              ) of the principal ultrafilter
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi η
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta x
            %li
              given an ultrafilter
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              on ultrafilters, the limit of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu U
              is the limit of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi β
                      %mi lim
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\beta \lim) U
          %p
            It is then a theorem that this
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi lim
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lim
            generates a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convergence+space"} convergence
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            that is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+space"} compact
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+space"} Hausdorff
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ultrafilter+principle"} ultrafilter principle
          %p
            Every compact Hausdorff space is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+space"} regular
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sober+space"} sober
            and so defines a compact regular locale. Again, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            gives us a converse: every compact regular locale is spatial and so comes from a compact Hausdorff space.
          %blockquote
            %p Probably this is also equivalent to the ultrafilter principle, but I need to check.
          %p
            Note that every compact Hausdorff space (topological or localic) is not only regular but also
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+space"} normal
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Hausdorff+spaces+are+normal"} compact Hausdorff spaces are normal
          %h2#algebras Compact Hausdorff spaces as algebras
          %p
            Throughout this section,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CH
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CH
            will be used to denote the category of compact Hausdorff spaces.
          %h3#the_space_of_ultrafilters The space of ultrafilters
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Bool
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Bool
            be the category of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+algebras"} Boolean algebras
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi Bool
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hom(-, \mathbf{2}): Bool^{op} \to Set
            has a left
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint"} adjoint
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo :
                  %mi Set
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi Bool
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P: Set \to Bool^{op}
            given by power sets, and we define the
            %strong ultrafilter monad
            to be the composite
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi P
                    %mo −
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta \coloneqq \hom(P -, \mathbf{2})
          %p
            For a set
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topologize
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta S
            by declaring a basic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+set"} open set
            to be one of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi F
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi β
                  %mi S
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{A} \coloneqq \{F \in \beta S: A \in F\}
          %p
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            a subset of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi ∅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{\emptyset}
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+set"} empty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{(-)}
            defines a Boolean algebra map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi β
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(S) \to P(\beta S)
          %p
            so that in particular
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ∩
                        %mi B
                      %mo ^
                    %mo =
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo ∩
                    %mover
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{A \cap B} = \hat{A} \cap \hat{B}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{A}
            form a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/basis"} basis
            of a topology.
          #rem.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              In fact,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{(-)}
              is the component at
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(S)
              of the counit of the adjunction
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mo ⊣
                      %mi hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \dashv \hom(-, \mathbf{2})
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Bool
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Bool^{op}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi S
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: S \to T
              is a function, the commutativity of the naturality square
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi P
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi T
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mover
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ^
                          %mtd
                            %mi P
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi β
                            %mi T
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mi P
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi f
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mi P
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi β
                                %mi f
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi P
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi S
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mover
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ^
                          %mtd
                            %mi P
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi β
                            %mi S
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    P(T) &amp; \stackrel{\widehat{(-)}}{\to} &amp; P(\beta T) \\
                    \\mathllap{P(f)} \downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow \mathrlap{P(\beta f)} \\
                    P(S) &amp; \overset{\widehat{(-)}}{\to} &amp; P(\beta S)
                    }
            %p
              implies that if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo =
                    %mover
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi β
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U = \hat{B} \in P(\beta T)
              is a basic (cl)open, then so is
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi β
                      %mi f
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi β
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mover
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mover
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi f
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi B
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ^
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\beta f)^{-1}(U) = P(\beta f)(\hat{B}) = \widehat{f^{-1}(B)}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta f
              is continuous.
          %p
            These results show that the monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                  %mo :
                  %mi Set
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta: Set \to Set
            lifts through the forgetful functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo :
                    %mi Top
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U: Top \to Set
          %p
            The
            %em unit
            of the monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
            is given componentwise by functions
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi prin
                    %mi X
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi β
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} prin_X: X \to \beta X
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi prin
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} prin_X
            takes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
            to the principal ultrafilter
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi prin
                    %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} prin_X(x) = \{A \in P(X): x \in A\}.
          %p
            It is evident that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi prin
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} prin_X
            is injective.
          #dense.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The injection
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi prin
                      %mi X
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi β
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} prin_X: X \to \beta X
              exhibits
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dense+subset"} dense subset
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi β
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta X
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{A}
              is a basic open neighborhood containing an ultrafilter
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is nonempty and hence contains some
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi prin
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in prin_X(x)
              or that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi prin
                        %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %mover
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} prin_X(x) \in \hat{A}
          %h3#ultrafilters_form_a_compact_hausdorff_space Ultrafilters form a compact Hausdorff space
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta S
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+space"} Hausdorff
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ,
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F, G
              be distinct ultrafilters, so there is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \subseteq S
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in F
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ¬
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg A \in G
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{A}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %mo ¬
                        %mi A
                      %mo ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{\neg A}
              are disjoint neighborhoods which contain
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              respectively.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta S
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+space"} compact
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              It is enough to show that if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}
              is a collection of opens such that the union of any finite subcollection is a proper subset, then the union of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}
              is also proper.
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}
              covers
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}
              consists of basic clopens
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{A}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}
              is a proper subset of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi β
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta S
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %mo ¬
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mn 1
                      %mo ^
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi …
                    %mo ∩
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %mo ¬
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mi n
                      %mo ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{\neg A_1} \cap \ldots \cap \widehat{\neg A_n}
              is nonempty, so that the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ¬
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg A
              generate a filter, which is contained in some ultrafilter
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              lies outside the union of all the
              = succeed "\u2018s." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{A}
          %h3#convergence Convergence
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a topological space, and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              an ultrafilter on the underlying set
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              %em converges
              to a point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              (in symbols,
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo ⇝
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \rightsquigarrow x
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neighborhood"} neighborhood filter
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_x
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              is contained in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
          %p
            Convergence defines a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation"} relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ξ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta(U X)
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U X
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is Hausdorff, then the relation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ξ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi
              is well-defined, or
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functional+relation"} functional
              (i.e., there is at most one point to which a given ultrafilter
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              converges).
          .proof
            %h6#proof_4 Proof
            %p
              If
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ≠
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \neq y
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in F
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \in F
              (otherwise
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ∅
                    %mo =
                    %mi U
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \emptyset = U \cap V
              would be an element of
              = succeed ")," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_x, N_y
              can be contained in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is compact, then the relation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ξ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+relation"} total
              (i.e., there exists a point to which a given ultrafilter
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              converges).
          .proof
            %h6#proof_5 Proof
            %p
              If not, then for each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              there is an open neighborhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_x
              that does not belong to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ¬
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg U_x \in F
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_{x_1}, \ldots, U_{x_n}
              covers
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ¬
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi x
                            %mn 1
                      %mo ∩
                      %mi …
                      %mo ∩
                      %mo ¬
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi x
                            %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mi ∅
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg U_{x_1} \cap \ldots \cap \neg U_{x_n} = \emptyset \in F
          #coun.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_6 Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is compact Hausdorff, then the function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ξ
                    %mo :
                    %mi β
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi: \beta(U X) \to X
              is continuous.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_6 Proof
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              be an open neighborhood of
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ξ
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi^{-1}(U)
              contains an open neighborhood of any of its points (i.e., ultrafilters
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              such that
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo ⇝
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \rightsquigarrow x
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_3
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separation+axioms"}> Hausdorff regular
              ), we may choose a neighborhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \in N_x
              whose closure
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar{V}
              is contained in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{V}
              is an open neighborhood of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi β
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta(U X)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi V
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mo ⊆
                      %msup
                        %mi ξ
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{V} \subseteq \xi^{-1}(U)
            %p
              For this, we must check that if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo ∈
                    %mover
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \in \hat{V}
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                      %mo ⇝
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \rightsquigarrow y
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \in U
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo ∈
                      %mo ¬
                      %mi U
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mo ¬
                      %mover
                        %mi V
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \in \neg U \subseteq \neg \bar{V}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ¬
                      %mover
                        %mi V
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi N
                        %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg \bar{V} \in N_y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo ⇝
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \rightsquigarrow y
              implies
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ¬
                      %mover
                        %mi V
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg \bar{V} \in G
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                      %mo ∈
                      %mover
                        %mi V
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \in \hat{V}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \in G
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                      %mo ∩
                      %mo ¬
                      %mover
                        %mi V
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                      %mo =
                      %mi ∅
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \cap \neg \bar{V} = \emptyset
          %h3#spaces_of_ultrafilters_are_universal Spaces of ultrafilters are universal
          #exist.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_7 Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is a set and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a compact Hausdorff space, then any function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi S
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: S \to X
              can be extended (along
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi prin
                        %mi S
                      %mo :
                      %mi S
                      %mo →
                      %mi β
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} prin_S: S \to \beta S
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mo :
                      %mi β
                      %mi S
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{f}: \beta S \to X
          .proof
            %h6#proof_7 Proof
            %p
              We define
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{f}
              to be the composite
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                    %mi S
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mi β
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi β
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi ξ
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta S \stackrel{\beta(f)}{\to} \beta (U X) \stackrel{\xi}{\to} X
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta(f)
              is continuous by Remark
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#rem"}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ξ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi
              is continuous by Proposition
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#coun"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi S
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi U
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi prin
                                  %mi S
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi prin
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi U
                                    %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mn 1
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi U
                                    %mi X
                          %mtd
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi β
                            %mi S
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mi β
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi f
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi β
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi U
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo →
                              %mi ξ
                          %mtd
                            %mi U
                            %mi X
                            %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    S &amp; \stackrel{f}{\to} &amp; U X &amp; &amp; \\
                    \\mathllap{prin_S} \downarrow &amp; &amp; \mathllap{prin_{U X}} \downarrow &amp; \searrow \mathrlap{1_{U X}} &amp; \\
                    \\beta S &amp; \underset{\beta (f)}{\to} &amp; \beta (U X) &amp; \underset{\xi}{\to} &amp; U X.
                    }
            %p
              The square commutes by naturality of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi prin
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} prin
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi prin
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} prin_{U X}(x)
              converges to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi N
                        %mi x
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi prin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_x \subseteq prin(x)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in V
              for every neighborhood
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi N
                        %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \in N_x
          #free.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              For any set
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi prin
                      %mi S
                    %mo :
                    %mi S
                    %mo →
                    %mi β
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} prin_S: S \to \beta S
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal
              among functions from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              to compact Hausdorff spaces. Hence the functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi Set
                    %mo →
                    %mi CH
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F: Set \to CH
              that takes
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              to the compact Hausdorff space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta S
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              to the forgetful functor
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi CH
                      %mo →
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CH \to Set
          .proof
            %h6#proof_8 Proof
            %p
              Proposition
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#exist"}
              shows that for any function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi S
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: S \to U X
              to a compact Hausdorff space, there exists continuous
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %mi β
                    %mi S
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g: \beta S \to X
              such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mi prin
                        %mi S
                      %mo =
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \circ prin_S = f
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo ′
                    %mo :
                    %mi β
                    %mi S
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g, g': \beta S \to X
              to a Hausdorff space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              agree on a dense subspace, in this case the subspace
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi prin
                      %mi S
                    %mo :
                    %mi S
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi β
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} prin_S : S \hookrightarrow \beta S
              by Proposition
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#dense"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi β
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta S
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi D
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi δ
                                  %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi β
                            %mi S
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                                %mi g
                                %mo ,
                                %mi g
                                %mo ′
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo ×
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    D &amp; \to &amp; X \\
                    \\downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow \mathrlap{\delta_X} \\
                    \\beta S &amp; \underset{\langle g, g' \rangle}{\to} &amp; X \times X,
                    }
            %p
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              contains a dense subspace
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                      %mo =
                      %mi β
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D = \beta S
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g'
              is all of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi β
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta S
          %h3#compact_hausdorff_spaces_are_monadic_over_sets Compact Hausdorff spaces are monadic over sets
          %p
            We recall hypotheses of Beck’s precise
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadicity+theorem"} monadicity theorem
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U: C \to D
            is monadic if and only if
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                has a left adjoint,
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                reflects isomorphisms: a morphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: X \to Y
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is an isomorphism if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi U
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi U
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U f: U X \to U Y
                is an isomorphism in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                has, and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                preserves, coequalizers of parallel pairs that are
                = succeed "-split." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mover
                        %munder
                          %mo →
                          %mi g
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mi f
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \stackrel{\overset{f}{\to}}{\underset{g}{\to}} Y
              %p
                is
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                %strong split
                if there is a coequalizer
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mi X
                      %mover
                        %munder
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %mi U
                            %mi g
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %mi U
                            %mi f
                      %mi U
                      %mi Y
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi h
                      %mi Z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U X \stackrel{\overset{U f}{\to}}{\underset{U g}{\to}} U Y \stackrel{h}{\to} Z
              %p
                that is split in
                = succeed ":" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo :
                      %mi Z
                      %mo →
                      %mi U
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i: Z \to U Y
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mo :
                      %mi U
                      %mi Y
                      %mo →
                      %mi U
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j: U Y \to U X
                such that
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mi h
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mn 1
                          %mi Z
