                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \times_Y R^{op} \to Y \times Y
              is also closed. This completes the proof.
          %h2#weak_versions Weak versions
          %p
            Every
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+space"} Hausdorff space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separation+axiom"} separation axiom
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_0
            version. A priori, this is a compact
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preregular+space"} preregular space
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+space"} regular
            = succeed "." do
              %strong compact regular space
          %p
            In the absence of the axiom of choice, and especially in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nice+category+of+spaces"} nice category of spaces
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+interval"} unit interval
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tychonoff+theorem"} Tychonoff theorem
            for an example of how the category of compact Hausdorff topological spaces might fail to be nice; see
            %a{:href => "https://www.fwaaldijk.nl/foundations%20of%20constructive%20mathematics.pdf"} Franka Waaldijk’s PhD thesis
            (pdf) for a thorough discussion of what is needed to make the unit interval a compact Hausdorff topological space.)
          %p
            The monadic definition, in particular, falls quite flat without some form of the axiom of choice; even
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excluded+middle"} excluded middle
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/COSHEP"} COSHEP
            are powerless here. In fact, it is quite consistent to assume that every ultrafilter is principal (a strong denial of the ultrafilter principle), in which case
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
            is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+monad"} identity monad
          %p
            On the other hand, it is the monadic definition that gives an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+category"} algebraic category
            with a nice relationship to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functor"} continuous
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#general General
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Hausdorff+spaces+are+normal"} compact Hausdorff spaces are normal
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subspaces+of+compact+Hausdorff+spaces+are+locally+compact"} open subspaces of compact Hausdorff spaces are locally compact
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subspaces+of+compact+Hausdorff+spaces+are+equivalently+compact+subspaces"} closed subspaces of compact Hausdorff spaces are equivalently compact subspaces
          %h3#StoneCechCompactification Stone–Čech compactification
          %p
            By general nonsense, every
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta S
            = succeed "-algebra," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                  %mo :
                  %mi Set
                  %mo →
                  %mi Comp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta: Set \to Comp
          %p
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Comp
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Comp \to Set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                  %mo :
                  %mi Top
                  %mo →
                  %mi Comp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta: Top \to Comp
            (identifying a set with its
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+space"} discrete space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Comp
                    %mo →
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Comp \to Top
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stone%E2%80%93%C4%8Cech+compactification"} Stone–Čech compactification
            functor (N.B.: for many authors, Stone–Čech compactification refers to the restriction of this functor to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tychonoff+spaces"} Tychonoff spaces
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi β
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to \beta X
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding"} embedding
            so that we have a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactification"} compactification
            in the technical sense).
          %p
            A classical construction of the Stone–Čech compactification starts with the unit
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval"} interval
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I =[0, 1]
            and proceeds to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codensity+monad"} codensity monad
            induced from the functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mi I
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi Top
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hom(-, I) \colon Top^{op} \to Set.
          %p
            The monad is given on objects by
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ↦
                    %msup
                      %mi I
                      %mrow
                        %mi hom
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi I
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \mapsto I^{\hom(X, I)}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar{X}
            be the closure of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
            of the unit
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi u
                      %mi X
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi I
                      %mrow
                        %mi hom
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi I
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u_X: X \to I^{\hom(X, I)}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar{X}
            is compact Hausdorff.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_8 Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tychonoff+space"} Tychonoff space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi u
                      %mi X
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi I
                      %mrow
                        %mi hom
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi I
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u_X: X \to I^{\hom(X, I)}
              is a subspace embedding, so that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cogenerator"} cogenerator
              in the category of Tychonoff spaces. (In particular,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi u
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u_C
              is an embedding if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is compact Hausdorff, so
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              is also a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cogenerator"} cogenerator
              in the category of compact Hausdorff spaces.)
          %p
            The proof is essentially
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urysohn%27s+lemma"} Urysohn's lemma
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tychonoff+space"} Tychonoff space
            and at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniform+space"} uniform space
            (noting that compact Hausdorff spaces are uniform spaces for a unique uniformity).
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_3 Theorem
            %p
              The natural map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mi X
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_X: X \to \bar{X}
              is universal among maps from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              to compact Hausdorff spaces, thus giving a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Top
                    %mo →
                    %mi Comp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top \to Comp
              to the (fully faithful) forgetful functor
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo :
                      %mi Comp
                      %mo →
                      %mi Top
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U: Comp \to Top
          .proof
            %h6#proof_11 Proof
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: X \to C
              be a map, where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is a compact Hausdorff space. Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              is a cogenerator in the category of compact Hausdorff spaces, the unit for the codensity monad
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi M
                        %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_I
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi u
                      %mi C
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi I
                      %mrow
                        %mi hom
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi C
                        %mo ,
                        %mi I
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u_C: C \to I^{\hom(C, I)},
            %p
              is a continuous injection (and hence a closed subspace embedding, since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is compact Hausdorff). Let
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi M
                        %mi I
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{f} = M_I(f)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mover
                                %mi f
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi C
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi I
                              %mrow
                                %mi hom
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi X
                                %mo ,
                                %mi I
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mi π
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mover
                                %mi f
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi u
                                  %mi C
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi I
                              %mrow
                                %mi hom
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi C
                                %mo ,
                                %mi I
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\hat{f}^{-1}(C) &amp; \to &amp; I^{\hom(X, I)} \\
                    \\mathllap{\pi} \downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow \mathrlap{\hat{f}} \\
                    C &amp; \underset{u_C}{\to} &amp; I^{\hom(C, I)}.
                    }
            %p
              From an evident naturality square for the unit
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi u
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi h
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mover
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h: X \to \hat{f}^{-1}(C)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi u
                      %mi X
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi I
                      %mrow
                        %mi hom
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi I
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u_X: X \to I^{\hom(X, I)}
              factors through the closed subspace
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mover
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ↪
                      %msup
                        %mi I
                        %mrow
                          %mi hom
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo ,
                          %mi I
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{f}^{-1}(C) \hookrightarrow I^{\hom(X, I)}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
              factors as
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mo ⊆
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \stackrel{i_X}{\to} \bar{X} \subseteq \hat{f}^{-1}(C)
            %p
              and since
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi π
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi h
                      %mo =
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi \circ h = f
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              factors through
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo :
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k: \bar{X} \to C
              such that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mi X
                      %mo =
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \circ i_X = f
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_X
              maps
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              onto a dense subspace of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar{X}
          %p
            We have a similar Stone–Čech compactification functor
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Loc
                    %mo →
                    %mi Comp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Loc \to Comp
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Comp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Comp
            is defined in terms of locales.
          %h3#category_of_compact_hausdorff_spaces Category of compact Hausdorff spaces
          %p
            The category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Comp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Comp
            of compact Hausdorff spaces and continuous maps is
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+category"}> Barr exact
                , since
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo :
                      %mi Comp
                      %mo →
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U: Comp \to Set
                is monadic,
            %li
              %p
                an
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensive+category"} extensive category
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+category"} total category
                (by monadicity over
                = succeed ")," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Set
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+category"} cototal category
                (because it is
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+category"} complete
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well-powered+category"} well-powered
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cogenerator"} cogenerator
                given by the unit interval
                = succeed ")." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi I
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I = [0, 1]
          %p
            From the first two properties, it follows that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Comp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Comp
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pretopos"} pretopos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Comp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Comp
            enjoys the same finitary exactness properties that hold in a
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Comp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Comp
          %p
            In (
            %a{:href => "#MarraReggio"}> Marra-Reggio 18
            ), the authors give a characterization of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Comp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Comp
            up to equivalence as the unique non-trivial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pretopos"} pretopos
            which is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well-pointed+category"} well-pointed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtrality"} filtral
            and admits all set-indexed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/copowers"} copowers
            of its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ETCS"} ETCS
          %blockquote
            %p
              the existence of infinite “discrete” objects. While the third axiom of ETCS postulates the existence of a natural numbers object, we prescribe filtrality which forbids the existence of infinite discrete objects. (
              %a{:href => "#MarraReggio"}> Marra-Reggio 18, p. 2
              )
          %p
            In the context of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ultracategories"} ultracategories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Comp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Comp
            is equivalent to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Fun
                      %mi RUlt
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fun_{RUlt}(\ast, Set)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie"}> Lurie, p. 4
            ).
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitary+pretopos"} infinitary pretopos
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/condensed+sets"} condensed sets
            is the completion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pretopos"} pretopos
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Hausdorff+spaces"} compact Hausdorff spaces
          %h3#relation_to_compactly_generated_topological_spaces Relation to compactly generated topological spaces
          %p
          #kSpacesAreTheColimitsInTopOfCompactHausdorffSpaces.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/k-spaces"} k-spaces
                are the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top#UniversalConstructions"} colimits in Top
                of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Hausdorff+spaces"} compact Hausdorff spaces
              %br/
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/k-space"} k-space
              (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#kSpace"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
              as formed in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              (according to
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "Top#DescriptionOfLimitsAndColimitsInTop"} this Prop.
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Hausdorff+spaces"} compact Hausdorff spaces
          (
          %a{:href => "#EscardoLawsonSimpson04"}> Escardo, Lawson &amp; Simpson 2004, Lem. 3.2 (v)
          )
          %p
            Such colimits of compact Hausdorff spaces are also equivalently
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+topological+spaces"} quotient topological spaces
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+Hausdorff+spaces"} locally compact Hausdorff spaces
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "locally+compact+topological+space#kSpacesAreTheQuotientSpacesOfLocallyCompactHausdorffSpaces"} there
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+space"}> compact space
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+space"} locally compact space
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+space"} compactly generated topological space
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+Hausdorff+space"} paracompact Hausdorff space
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dyadic+compactum"} dyadic compactum
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pyknotic+set"} pyknotic set
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saunders+MacLane"}> Saunders MacLane
                , §VI.9 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categories+for+the+Working+Mathematician"} Categories for the Working Mathematician
                %strong 5
                Springer (1971, second ed. 1997) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-1-4757-4721-8"}> doi:10.1007/978-1-4757-4721-8
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#MarraReggio
              %p
                Vincenzo Marra, Luca Reggio,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A characterisation of the category of compact Hausdorff spaces
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1808.09738"} arXiv:1808.09738
            %li#Lurie
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Ultracategories
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.harvard.edu/~lurie/papers/Conceptual.pdf"} pdf
            %li#CCGM24
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Felix+Cherubini"}> Felix Cherubini
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thierry+Coquand"} Thierry Coquand
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Freek+Geerligs"} Freek Geerligs
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hugo+Moeneclaey"} Hugo Moeneclaey
                %em A Foundation for Synthetic Stone Duality
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.03203"}> arXiv:2412.03203
                )
          %p
            Relation to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+spaces"} compactly generated topological spaces
          %ul
            %li#EscardoLawsonSimpson04
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mart%C3%ADn+Escard%C3%B3"}> Martín Escardó
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jimmie+Lawson"} Jimmie Lawson
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alex+Simpson"} Alex Simpson
              = succeed "," do
                %em Comparing Cartesian closed categories of (core) compactly generated spaces
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.topol.2004.02.011"} doi:10.1016/j.topol.2004.02.011
